[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1279","stub":{"id":"1279","section":"Glenwood to Lackawanna","altname":"","river":"Cazenovia Creek, W.Branch","difficulty":"IIstandoutIV","states":["USA-NYO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"261","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"108138","location":{"latitude":"42.6148986816406","longitude":"-78.6551971435547"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"113380","location":{"latitude":"42.8446998596191","longitude":"-78.8050994873047"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"15","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"879091","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879517","description":"This is the twisting falls underneath the bridge in the town of Colden. Caz gauge at Ebenezer was 750 and dropping.","caption":"Colden Falls","poi_name":"Colden Falls","subject":"","author":"Max Brown","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879091","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879091"}},{"id":"879092","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879518","description":"This is the twisting falls underneath the bridge in the town of Colden. Caz gauge at Ebenezer was 750 and dropping.","caption":"Colden Falls Picture 2","poi_name":"Colden Falls","subject":"","author":"Max Brown","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879092","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879092"}},{"id":"879093","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"879519","description":"This is the twisting falls underneath the bridge in the town of Colden. Caz gauge at Ebenezer was 1100 and rising. Jay and I didn't think it was high enough at 750 and dropping, so we had a beer and some food at the Colden Inn, and sure enough it rained pretty had for about an hour and we were able to put on at 8pm for some action from Colden, down to the Buffalo Ski Club bridge.","caption":"Colden Falls Picture 3","poi_name":"Colden Falls","subject":"","author":"Max Brown","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879093","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879093"}}],"detail":{"id":"1279","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Lat/longitude coordinates are approximate, from TopoZone. The last few miles of this reach are on the Cazenovia proper.\n\nCameron Brown helped out with:\n\nOn 5/26/11, Jay and I paddled from above the falls in Colden, about 2 miles down to the Buffalo Ski Club bridge. The falls looked runnable but low at 750 and dropping, and the rest of the run would have been too low. After some more rain, the river shot up, and we put on at about 1100 and rising.\n\nThe falls was fun (even though I rolled once halfway down and again at the bottom), and Jay had a clean run. After that, it was 2 miles of swifts, some small surf waves, some wood, and 1 lowhead dam. At this level it was an easy boof; at higher levels it might be a decent sized hole, and at very high levels, might even be a nice surf wave. There is an eddy on the right above the dam.\n\nSince we put on at 8 pm, we didn't have enough time to make it down to West Falls. From our run, there wasn't anything rated V, but maybe there are other drops between Glenwood and Lackawanna that are difficult. I would give Colden Falls a IV rating and the rest of the run II. - Max\n\n**Western New York Area Reaches**\n\n[Beaver Meadow Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/5749/) [Canadaway Creek (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/6205/) [Canadaway Creek (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/6246/)\n\n[Canaseraga Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1270/) [Cattaraugus Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1278/) [Cattaraugus Creek, S. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1277/)\n\n[Cazenovia Creek, W. Branch (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1279/)[Cazenovia Creek, W. Branch (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3987/) [Chautauqua Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1283/)\n\n[Clear Creek, N. Br.](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/5753/) [Conesus Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/5203/) [Eighteenmile Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1299/)\n\n[Eighteenmile Creek, S. Br.](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/5051/) [Ellicott Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10882/) [Genesee (Letchworth)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1308/)\n\n[Honeoye Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1319/) [Keshequa Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1331/) [Little Chautauqua Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/6245/)\n\n[Murder Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4292/) [Niagara](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1360/) [Oak Orchard Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1364/)\n\n[Oatka Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1365/) [Rushford Lake Outlet](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1397/) [Sugar Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/2702/)\n\n[Twentymile Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1447/)\n\n**[Google Map of New York 